  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which model represents the division problem below?\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{1}{4}=8\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate $2÷\\frac{1}{4}$, we need to divide each of $2$ wholes into $4$ equal parts, as shown below. This gives us the corresponding model for the given division problem.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129499/assets/227e3080de354aa93af71f70747ab31f7673b6e6e9d0591c84dfafcfe56edc56.png)\n\n \n\nWe get $2\\times 4=8$ pieces in total.",
